    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nLocated 1.5km south of Bray Main Street, Richmond Way is a small development of only 10 apartments that were developed c. 2007. Thoughtfully designed at the time of construction, No. 5 is a two-bedroom dual aspect apartment occupying a first-floor position. The bright interior is practical for modern day living and the accommodation is scheduled on one level measuring 71 sq. m approx. \n\nOn approach, a gravelled car park provides each resident with a secure surface level parking space. Entering the development, a communal stairwell rises to the upper floors. Passing through the hall door of No. 5, the entrance hall comprises wood flooring and shelved hot-press. To the right of the corridor there are two double bedrooms, both include wood floors and fitted wardrobes while the larger of the two has the added benefit of an en-suite shower room. On the opposite side of the hallway there is access to a tiled bathroom complete with a whb, W.C, and bath with overhead shower. Further along, a door opens to an impressive triple aspect open plan living/kitchen/dining room which acts as the main focal point. This large room incorporates wood flooring, recess lighting, while in the kitchen area there is a range of cabinetry, tiled splashback, and integrated appliances include an oven, hob, and extractor fan. \n\nEach apartment within the development profits from a communal roof top terrace which is decked and has 360-degree views spanning from Bray Head across to the two Sugarloaf's, Carrigoona Commons, Djouce Mountains, Glencree and Carrickgollgan. This unexpected gem is accessed from the landing in the communal hallway via a spiral staircase with feature glass bricks. \n\nThe location of Richmond Way is one of convenience with local shops and Supermarkets in the immediate vicinity while slightly further afield is the Main Street offering a variety of eateries and shops. There are a host of well-regarded junior and secondary schools close by and there are several sport and leisure facilities to choose from including Shoreline Leisure Complex. For the outdoor adventure enthusiasts, walks can be enjoyed along the charming Victorian Promenade, Bray Head, the Sugarloaf's, or in nearby Killruddery Estate. The development also benefits from being within close proximity to transport links including the N11/M50 routeway, frequent bus services, and Bray DART Station."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - 6.37m x 1.44m\n\n\nLiving Dining Room - 7.38m x 3.94m\n\n\nKitchen - 1.68m x 1.92m\n\n\nBedroom 1 - 3.36m x 4.02m\n\n\nEn-Suite - 1.93m x 1.79m\n\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.36m x 2.77m\n\n\nBathroom - 1.68m x 3.08m\n\n\n"
